From b2739db54765899fc51e91b1c5f2761c9b451d26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:07:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(js): embedder filesystem mounts and port streams for
 access-controlled sandboxes

Expose what the core already has, so an application embedding the SDK can
decide every guest filesystem and network call itself:

- SandboxOptions.mounts and .storage: the core's mountHost/storageHost.
  Each guest filesystem call under a mount reaches the embedder as one
  request (the existing host-filesystem bridge), which can allow it,
  answer it, or refuse it with EACCES.
- Node SDK workers install the host-filesystem bridge, as browser workers
  already do, so mounts work in Node too.
- Ports.fetch(port, request) and Ports.connect(port): the core's
  handleHttpRequest/connectTcp, to reach a guest listener without a
  ServiceWorker or a host port.
- Export ./host-filesystem (isHostFileSystemRequest,
  respondToHostFileSystem) for embedders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
