+### Talk to a guest listener without a host port
+
+`ports.fetch()` sends one HTTP request to a guest TCP listener and returns its
+response; `ports.connect()` opens a raw byte stream (WebSockets, database
+protocols). Neither needs a ServiceWorker or a host port, and the embedder sees
+every request it forwards. Both need `network: { mode: "http" }` or `"wisp"`.
+
+```js
+const sandbox = await wasmer.sandboxes.create({
+  packages: ["python/python"],
+  network: { mode: "http", peers: [] },
+});
+await sandbox.command("python", ["-m", "http.server", "8080"]).spawn();
+await sandbox.ports.wait(8080);
+const response = await sandbox.ports.fetch(8080, new Request("http://guest/"));
+
+const { readable, writable, close } = sandbox.ports.connect(8080);
+```
+
+## Embedder filesystems (experimental)
+
+`mounts` and `storage` let the application serve a guest directory itself.
+Every guest filesystem call under a mount (`stat`, `readDir`, `open`, `read`,
+`write`, …) reaches the application as one request through
+`globalThis.__wasmerHandleFileSystemRpc`, so it can authorize each operation
+against its own access policy: return the result, or an error with a code
+such as `EACCES` (the guest sees a permission error) or `ENOENT`.
+
+```js
+import { isHostFileSystemRequest, respondToHostFileSystem } from "@wasmer/sdk/host-filesystem";
+
+globalThis.__wasmerHandleFileSystemRpc = (message) => {
+  if (!isHostFileSystemRequest(message)) return false;
+  respondToHostFileSystem(message, myFiles.handle(message.mount, message.method, message.args));
+  return true;
+};
+
+const sandbox = await wasmer.sandboxes.create({
+  packages: ["python/python"],
+  mounts: [{ path: "/data", mount: 1, readOnly: true }],
+  storage: { mount: 2 }, // `/workspace`, including `sandbox.fs`
+});
+```
+
+The guest blocks while the application answers, so answer from a thread
+whose event loop is free. Node and browser SDK workers both install the
+bridge. `tests/embedder-mounts.test.mjs` shows a complete read-only policy.
+
 ## Examples
 
 Run these from the repository root after `npm run build` in `js/`:
